    {
      "name": "Business Overview",
      "id": "3a150366-6cef-4dc3-be5b-5f41b44093b5",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        0,
        -280
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## AP intake | One shared upload / readonly Gmail flow\nArchive & Read \u2192 Invoice Analysis Agent \u2192 deterministic validation and approval policy. Eligible EUR gross totals below 10,000 are approved; all exceptions and larger totals go to human review. Final decisions hand off to independent workflow 02; pending tasks notify the reviewer. No waiting for a human inside this workflow.",
        "width": 2800,
        "height": 180
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "Current Scope",
      "id": "bd9a2ffd-432b-433f-8e0f-fc4c0c18404f",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        0,
        490
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Current Phase02 flow | Derived from v8; v7 and v8 preserved\nPython owns validation, duplicate checks, immutable review revisions, durable events and notification recovery. The Agent extracts; it never approves. Historical pending tasks are not automatically approved.\n\nApproved snapshots appear in the Web export register. Users select records and download a combined Excel file; the batch-ready event also enters workflow 02. Approval, file generation and notification statuses remain separate. Local Mailpit only; no accounting submission or payment. Bind the existing readonly Gmail and AP header credentials. Retry saved IDs; never recreate business decisions to hide failures.",
        "width": 2800,
        "height": 230
      }
    },
